        "description": "Exclusion of other causes of spastic paraplegia by neuroimaging and metabolic testing",
        "category": "supportive",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": true
      },
      {
        "id": "neuroimaging-findings",
        "description": "MRI showing mild corticospinal tract atrophy or nonspecific white matter changes",
        "category": "minor",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      },
      {
        "id": "family-history",
        "description": "Consanguinity or affected siblings consistent with autosomal recessive inheritance",
        "category": "supportive",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      }
    ],
    "minimumForDiagnosis": "Progressive lower limb spasticity with genetic confirmation of biallelic VPS13D pathogenic variants and exclusion of other etiologies",
    "notes": "Genetic testing is essential for definitive diagnosis; clinical presentation may overlap with other hereditary spastic paraplegias."
